   "format": "mcq",
   "stem": {
      "text": "Let F be the antiderivative of \\( f(x) = \\sec^{2}{\\left(2 x \\right)} \\) with \\( F(0) = 1 \\). Find the exact value of \\( F\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{8}\\right) \\)."
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": [
         "Rational",
         3,
         2
      ]
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Let \\( u = 2 x \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Multiply",
            2,
            "x"
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "Then \\( du = 2 \\, dx \\), so \\( dx = \\frac{1}{2} \\, du \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            1,
            2
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Since \\( F(\\frac{\\pi}{8}) = F(0) + \\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{8}} \\sec^{2}{\\left(2 x \\right)} \\, dx \\), convert the limits: \\( x = 0 \\) gives \\( u = 0 \\) and \\( x = \\frac{\\pi}{8} \\) gives \\( u = \\frac{\\pi}{4} \\), so the integral becomes \\( \\int_{0}^{\\frac{\\pi}{4}} \\frac{\\sec^{2}{\\left(u \\right)}}{2} \\, du \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
            [
               "Power",
               [
                  "Sec",
                  "u"
               ],
               2
            ],
            2
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 4,
         "text": "An antiderivative of \\( \\frac{\\sec^{2}{\\left(u \\right)}}{2} \\) is \\( \\frac{\\tan{\\left(u \\right)}}{2} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Divide",
            [
               "Tan",
               "u"
            ],
            2
         ]
      },
      {
         "step": 5,
         "text": "The integral is \\( \\frac{1}{2} - \\left(0\\right) = \\frac{1}{2} \\), so \\( F(\\frac{\\pi}{8}) = 1 + \\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{3}{2} \\).",
         "mathjson": [
            "Rational",
            3,
            2
         ]
      }
   ],
